  "id": "object-relations",
  "term": "object relations",
  "definition": "In cognition, object relations refers to perceiving how objects are positioned relative to one another rather than only relative to the body. This involves allocentric coding, such as judging the distance and orientation between objects to support spatial representation and action planning.",
